@startuml syscall-interposition
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam rectangleBorderThickness 2
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam packageBorderThickness 2

title Syscall Interposition: bwrap vs gVisor

package "**bwrap / namespace** — Shared Kernel" as P1 #FFEAA7 {
    rectangle "🤖 Agent" as A1 #74b9ff
    rectangle "🐧 Linux Kernel\n//(shared with host)//" as K1 #ff7675
    rectangle "💥 Kernel Exploit\n→ **ESCAPE**" as E1 #d63031

    A1 -right-> K1 : syscall (SYS_mmap, ...)
    K1 -right-> E1 : <color:red>CVE exploit</color>
}

package "**gVisor** — Syscall Interposition" as P2 #DFE6E9 {
    rectangle "🤖 Agent" as A2 #74b9ff
    rectangle "🛡️ gVisor Sentry\n//(Go process)//\nintercepts · emulates · rejects" as S2 #00b894
    rectangle "🐧 Host Kernel\n//(filtered calls only)//" as K2 #b2bec3

    A2 -right-> S2 : syscall (SYS_mmap, ...)
    S2 -right-> K2 : <color:green>safe calls only</color>
}

P1 -[hidden]down- P2

note bottom of P2
  Even if a reverse shell starts inside gVisor:
  • ""--network=none"" blocks all network access
  • Sentry blocks kernel exploits from reaching the host
end note

@enduml
